		<dc:title id="title">Hand and Ring</dc:title>
		<meta property="file-as" refines="#title">Hand and Ring</meta>
		<dc:subject id="subject-1">Detective and mystery stories</dc:subject>
		<meta property="authority" refines="#subject-1">LCSH</meta>
		<meta property="term" refines="#subject-1">sh85037260</meta>
		<meta property="schema:genre">Fiction</meta>
		<meta property="schema:genre">Mystery</meta>
		<meta id="collection-1" property="belongs-to-collection">Mr. Gryce</meta>
		<meta property="collection-type" refines="#collection-1">series</meta>
		<meta property="group-position" refines="#collection-1">4</meta>
		<meta property="schema:abstract">
			<p>When a conversation about how to commit the perfect murder is followed within minutes by a murder that mirrors the conversation, detectives are faced with confusion and misdirection by a diamond ring and the woman’s dying words “Hand! Ring!”.</p>
		</meta>
		<dc:description>
			&lt;p&gt;A conversation on the steps of a quiet courthouse in Sibley, New York turns to a chilling topic: how to commit the perfect, undetectable murder. A mysterious stranger declares that the secret lies in striking a blow in a busy thoroughfare using a weapon found on the spot, allowing the tracks of innocent passersby to naturally erase those of the killer.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;Then minutes later, just yards away from where this conversation took place, a deaf widow is found brutally struck down in her dining room in the exact fashion the stranger had just described. The dying woman’s last words, "Hand! Ring! Ring! Hand!", only confuse and misdirect the young detectives until Detective Gryce arrives.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;The author, &lt;a href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/anna-katharine-green"&gt;Anna Katherine Green&lt;/a&gt;, is known as the “mother of the detective novel”:her first novel predates &lt;a href="https://standardebooks.org/ebooks/arthur-conan-doyle"&gt;Arthur Cannon Doyle’s&lt;/a&gt; first &lt;a href="https://standardebooks.org/collections/sherlock-holmes"&gt;Sherlock Holmes&lt;/a&gt; novel by nearly a decade. Her detective stories have the classic elements of attention to clues, police procedure, and brilliant insight into human nature.&lt;/p&gt;
			&lt;p&gt;This is the fourth in the &lt;a href="https://standardebooks.org/collections/mr-gryce"&gt;Detective Gryce&lt;/a&gt; series, which totals thirteen novels. In this story, Detective Gryce does not come into the picture until near the end, where he plays a critical role identifying a key overlooked suspect.&lt;/p&gt;
		</dc:description>
